Rocky pushed back against the theory that he&#8217;s the reason that Rihanna hasn&#8217;t released a new album this decade due to their relationship and having three kids together.

&#8220;Nah,&#8221; he replied. &#8220;Yo, she in the studio right now. Yeah, I said it. Sorry, babe. Like, bro, she working. She cooking, no funny s&#8211;t. Damn, I&#8217;ma get in trouble for this.&#8221;

Billboard has reached out to Ri&#8217;s reps for comment.

There hasn&#8217;t been much movement when it comes to Rihanna&#8217;s publicized plans for new music. The superstar&#8217;s last release came as a contribution to the Smurfs Movie soundtrack with &#8220;Friend of Mine&#8221; in 2025.

The Navy was hyped to see Rihanna back in the studio earlier this year, when she posted footage from a recording session on social media in a day-in-the-life montage. &#8220;I have to go to the studio after this,” Rihanna said in the February clip. &#8220;And I have to make a Mardi Gras costume for my son after the studio … Longest day ever.&#8221;

Elsewhere in Jason Lee&#8217;s interview with Rocky, the host recalled a time when he bumped into Rocky and RiRi around 4:30 a.m. ET at a Walgreens, where the couple was having a Nerf gun fight in the aisles of the store. &#8220;There was nobody else in the store at first, but us, and y&#8217;all were two kids acting a damn fool, and it was the funniest thing,&#8221; Lee said.

Rihanna&#8217;s last album arrived in 2016 with ANTI , which spent two weeks atop the  Billboard 200.  Rihanna made her return to the stage in July when she appeared at Jay-Z&#8217;s Extra Innings show at Yankee Stadium and performed &#8220;Run This Town&#8221; and &#8220;Bitch Better Have My Money.&#8221;

